SECOND FINDING, PRE-EXISTING AND MEASURED ON A CLEAN HEAD WORKTREE:
  AC-EDMB3 was RED at HEAD independently of this window's change - the suite
  run in a pristine worktree of HEAD read AC-EDMB3 FAIL with the same cause.
  compose() read the borrowed-stamp origin only from a RECORDED ancestor, so
  a document that records none (which is what the live document holds)
  composed WITHOUT the --stamp-from line the criterion requires. compose()
  now accepts the source it actually borrowed from and that source wins, so
  the line cannot disappear again. No criterion was relaxed for this.

THE ONE CRITERION THAT HAD TO CHANGE, AND WHY IT IS STILL LOAD-BEARING:
  AC-EDMC4 in test_suite_matrix_reconcile_table_shape.py asserted
  evidence_source == "walk" for a walk-only reading. That exact value was
  only ever true while the real pile could NOT answer; it now truthfully
  reads "walk-leg". The assertion is now: the word is in ("walk","walk-leg"),
  is never "explicit", and the CLI echo is compared to that same exact word
  instead of a substring - so a silent merge of the two evidence sources,
  which is the whole point of AC-EDMC4, still reddens.

